  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Development updates</p><h1>Release notes</h1><p>Product changes are recorded here without implying that an installer has been released.</p></header>
  <div class="prose"><div class="notice"><p><strong>No installer release is available.</strong> RepoReady has no tested Windows client release and no certified application releases to download.</p></div><h2>Static discovery preview</h2><p><time datetime="2026-10-14">14 October 2026</time> · Website development</p><ul><li>Static discovery pages describe candidate apps across AI, productivity, media, and utilities.</li><li>Drafts clearly separate upstream research from RepoReady testing and certification.</li><li>The website explains two equally supported paths: direct standalone downloads when approved, and optional desktop management when available.</li><li>Trust, privacy, license, and support pages describe the current boundaries.</li></ul><p>Future release notes will identify actual approved versions, tested platforms, limitations, and artifact availability. See the <a href="https://github.com/Pranoym17/RepoReady">source repository</a> for implementation history.</p></div>
</SiteLayout>
